     A                                  1  2'MODIFY HELP -'
     A                                  3  2'THE "MODIFY" FUNCTION LETS YOU MOD-
     A                                      IFY THE EXISTING LINES OF A SEQUENC-
     A                                      E. YOU '
     A                                  4  1'CANNOT ADD NEW LINES TO THE END OF-
     A                                       THE SEQUENCE.'
     A                                  5  2'AFTER THE LINES APPEAR ON THE SCRE-
     A                                      EN SIMPLY MAKE YOUR CHANGES. YOUR C-
     A                                      HANGES'
     A                                  6  1'DO NOT TAKE EFFECT UNTIL YOU PRESS'
     A                                  6 36'"MAKE CHANGES". AT THIS TIME THE D-
     A                                      ATABASE IS'
     A                                  7  1'UPDATED WITH YOUR CHANGES AND YOUR'
     A                                  7 36'SCREEN IS RE-DISPLAYED SHOWING THE'
     A                                  7 71'CHANGES.'
     A                                  9  2'EDITING FUNCTIONS ARE AVAILABLE IN'
     A                                  9 37'THIS MODE. THE FIRST TWO POSITIONS'
     A                                  9 72'OF THE'
     A                                 10  1'LINE ARE USED FOR THE EDIT FUNCTIO-
     A                                      N. THE EDIT FUNCTIONS ARE "I*" "D*"-
     A                                       "M*" "C*".'
     A                                 12  2'I* IS THE INSERT FUNCTION. THIS LE-
     A                                      TS YOU INSERT NEW LINES BETWEEN 2'
     A                                 12 70'OTHER'
     A                                 13  1'LINES. YOU CAN INSERT UP TO 10 LIN-
     A                                      ES AT A TIME. IF YOU POSITION THE'
     A                                 13 69'CURSOR AT'
     A                                 14  1'LINE 20 AND TYPE "I*", YOU ARE REQ-
     A                                      UESTING THE PROGRAM TO LET YOU INSE-
     A                                      RT LINES'
     A                                 15  1'BEFORE LINE 20. IF THE LINE RIGHT'
     A                                 15 35'BEFORE 20 IS LINE 10 YOU WILL BE A-
     A                                      BLE TO ADD'
     A                                 16  1'THE LINES 11 12 13 14 15 16 17 18'
     A                                 16 35'19. AFTER TYPING IN YOUR NEW LINES'
     A                                 16 70'AND'
     A                                 17  1'PRESSING "Enter", THE LINES ARE IN-
     A                                      SERTED AND YOU RETURN TO "MODIFY"'
     A                                 17 69'MODE.'
     A                                 19  2'D* IS THE DELETE FUNCTION. THIS LE-
     A                                      TS YOU DELETE LINES OF THE SEQUENCE-
     A                                      . MORE'
     A                                 20  1'THAN 1 LINE CAN BE DELETED AT ONCE'
     A                                 20 36'BY TYPING "D*" ON MORE THAN 1 LINE-
     A                                      . IF YOU'
     A                                 21  1'WISH TO DELETE LINES 50 AND 80 TYP-
     A                                      E "D*" IN THE FIRST TWO POSITIONS'
     A                                 21 69'ON BOTH OF'
     A                                 22  1'THESE LINES. A LINE CAN ALSO BE DE-
     A                                      LETED BY LEAVING IT BLANK.'
